                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Statement to the press issued by the British Embassy
                        January 11, 1915</hi>
                </head>
                <p>It is understood that certain American and Italian shipping lines are refusing to
                    carry goods consigned by name to Swiss firms, and that this refusal has been
                    attributed in some quarters to some suggestion or action on the part of the
                    British authorities. There is no foundation whatever for the latter statement;
                    the British Government are on the contrary most anxious that no restrictions
                    whatever should be placed in the way of articles intended for <hi
                        rendition="#italic">bona fide</hi> consumption in Switzerland.</p>
            </div>
